<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bishop</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as episcopal</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A bishop is a senior member of the Christian clergy who oversees a diocese and its priests. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksumite Empire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frumentius">Frumentius</a> became the first bishop of Aksum after the adoption of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a> bishops were key royal agents who supplied revenue and troops, and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> the church hierarchy was integral to colonial government in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bishop.jpg" alt="Bishop" width="228" height="750" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eveque_de_Laon,_Barth%C3%A9l%C3%A9my_de_Jur.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
